This probably ends up as a YANI thread sooner or later but I'm curious 
why people think Gehennom in general is so boring (I do too, don't 
worry :-). I spent some time thinking about how it could be different 
(without changing too much) and in the end I'm convinced it's pretty 
cleverly thought out as it is actually.
Let's take the levels as an example. We probably should have 1-3 (at 
random) levels between each special level. As it is we have what, 11, 
special levels that usually have a few "normal" levels apart. The 
special levels have to situate between this and that level pretty much 
making it a decent random scene. Especially as something like Vlad's 
stairs can exist on another special level.
So maybe we should think about what feels wrong and see if we can come 
up something nifty from that.

Let's see now...

1) Boring, kinda too easy (own fault really as I overprepare then). But 
it would be fun if the named daemons didn't escape to the stairs but 
instead level teleported to some level and ganged up on you later on 
:-).

2) No teleporting on far too many levels. I don't mind not being able 
to teleport into certain structures (wizard's tower, Orcustown etc) but 
I would love to be able to teleport from elsewhere on the level to 
elsewhere on the level. That would speed up the no-teleport levels 
nicely without breaking things.

3) Bloody maze. With magic mapping I can just barely stand it. Maybe 
more junctions so you could easily get from point A to point B.

?) What annoys you?


